Local changes: resolved standalone manifest; optional TCP socket configuration callback before bind/listen; negotiated pointer capability callback to the authenticated display; format-data drain callback for bounded clipboard responses; AUDIO_INPUT channel recycle for stopping the microphone.
All protocol dependencies remain pinned to the same upstream revision.
Rebased 2026-10-15 from bf019ca502d1e52616853a5ded68c885cec1e322 onto master 7b976a6965c96c76ff949313e174ea55dada8c44 (upstream #2102 EGFX frame-ACK ceiling, #2111, #1985 offers_display_control); every local change below re-applied unchanged, none dropped. Upstream did not change sound.rs or ironrdp-rdpsnd, so the RDPSND format order, PCM preference, zero timestamps and wave/credit handling are untouched.
EGFX frame window: the egfx FrameTracker is the only credit gate. The bridge sets its adaptive window with set_max_frames_in_flight. Local change (2026-10-17): activation no longer applies #2102's client core Frame Acknowledge capability (MS-RDPRFX surface-command frame markers) to EGFX, because Windows 10 mstsc's value held the window at two frames, about 20 fps over a ~33 ms RTT path; RDPGFX has its own FrameAcknowledge flow control. The advertised value is recorded and exposed by take_client_frame_ack_capability() for the bridge's connection summary. frame_ack_limit_tests cover the recorded value; the egfx set_client_frame_ack_limit API is unchanged and the gfx legacy-factory test and bridge regression client_frame_ack_ceiling_bounds_the_adaptive_window_through_one_gate still exercise it.
Generic event diagnostics omit payload Debug values, including clipboard, desktop and audio bytes.
Classic bitmap subregions: count a short final shared-stride row with div_ceil; wire-decode regression runs via bridge/tests/bitmap_wire.rs.
Display refresh/suppression callbacks propagate to authenticated handlers; a bounded refresh epoch invalidates bitmap diff cache only for complete current desktop updates.
CLIPRDR input is bounded before SVC reassembly: per-connection fragment accounting caps declared and accumulated bytes, rejects unsupported compression and malformed sequences; wire regressions run through bridge/tests/clipboard_wire.rs.
CLIPRDR size bound raised to 32 MiB + 4 KiB + 8 bytes for clipboard images (packed DIB plus header). A well-formed message over the bound is skipped chunk by chunk without buffering and logged once with only its declared size; the session continues, and a skipped Format Data Response is replaced by a failed one so the request it answered is still answered in order. Malformed or compressed sequences still end the connection; regressions run through bridge/tests/clipboard_wire.rs.
Pointer cache size: RdpServerDisplay::pointer_cache_capabilities(max_size, cache_size), whose default forwards to pointer_capabilities, passes the client's negotiated pointerCacheSize to the authenticated display at each activation.
AUDIO_INPUT recycle (microphone stop, MS-RDPEAI has no stop PDU): ServerEvent::RdpeaiRecycle closes the open AUDIO_INPUT DVC, which runs the backend's on_close and releases the client's microphone, and creates a fresh channel from the factory so a later Open needs no reconnect; ignored (debug) when no AUDIO_INPUT channel is open. ConnectionState tracks the replacement id because DRDYNVC forgets a closed pre-registered type, and the existing ServerEvent::Rdpeai arm prefers it. Capture data the client sent before it processed the Close is dropped for that channel id until the client's Close arrives (bounded list of 8), because the pinned DRDYNVC server treats data for a removed channel as a fatal error. Logic in rdpeai_recycle.rs; RDPSND, EGFX and CLIPRDR arms untouched; regressions run through bridge/tests/microphone_wire.rs. Upstream candidate (WP-15 follow-up).
